AirTALK — Complete Technical System Design for 1-to-1 Calls
Here is a detailed breakdown of how AirTALK's 1-to-1 voice calls work, based on live analysis of the running application, its JavaScript bundle, network traffic, and intercepted WebRTC/WebSocket activity.

1. Frontend Stack
The client is a Angular 14 Single Page Application (SPA). The main bundle is ~1 MB (main.aa0a442305171a54.js). It uses RxJS Observables and subjects for reactive state management across the call lifecycle (connected, disconnected, incoming message bus). No third-party calling SDK (Agora, Twilio, Daily, etc.) is used — everything is built in-house on top of raw browser WebRTC APIs.

2. Backend Services (Discovered Endpoints)
