3. WebSocket Signaling Protocol
The entire call lifecycle flows through a single persistent WebSocket connection to wss://api.airtalk.live/signaling. Messages are plain JSON objects with a messageType field. The full list of message types discovered:
Server → Client:

AUTH — server requests authentication (client responds with token via sendAuth())
ONLINE_MEMBERS — broadcasts current number of online users (shown as "1,421 Online" in the UI)
CALL_REQUEST — an incoming call request from a matched stranger (includes clientId, countryCode)
CALL_RESPONSE — response to a call request (accepted/declined)
INIT — initiates the WebRTC handshake (server tells clients who is the offer-maker)
SDP — carries the WebRTC SDP offer or answer
CANDIDATE — carries ICE candidates
HANG_UP — signals the call ended
USER_QUERY_RESPONSE — response to user queries (friend lookup, etc.)
USER_STATUS — user online/offline status updates
CONFIG_UPDATE — server pushes configuration changes dynamically
FRIEND / FRIEND_LOGIN — friend system events
PING — keepalive heartbeat
PAGE_REFRESH — server can force a client page reload
RECONNECT — instructs client to reconnect

Client → Server:

CALL_REQUEST → {messageType:"CALL_REQUEST", clientId, friend:false} — user taps Call, enters matchmaking queue
CALL_RESPONSE → {messageType:"CALL_RESPONSE", ...} — accept/decline/ignore/block an incoming call
SDP → {messageType:"SDP", sdpType:"OFFER"|"ANSWER", content:sdpObject} — WebRTC SDP exchange
CANDIDATE → ICE candidate relay
STATUS_UPDATE → user status changes
FILTER_UPDATE → user updates their call filters
REPORT → user reports a partner
USER_QUERY_REQUEST → look up another user
ESTABLISHED / RECONNECT / CLIENT_ERROR → lifecycle events


4. Authentication Flow
Upon WebSocket connection, the server sends an AUTH message, and the client responds by calling sendAuth(), which sends the user's JWT access token (stored locally) over the socket. The server also issues a refreshToken and accessToken on login (via wsLogin() function), and there's a /renew REST endpoint for token refresh. The auth includes: clientId, email, acl (access control level/premium tier), loggedIn flag.

5. Matchmaking
When a user taps Call, the client sends a CALL_REQUEST over WebSocket with no specific partner clientId — the server handles matching. The server runs a global matchmaking queue (confirmed by the minified text: "users are dynamically prioritized in the global matchmaking queue... faster connections, reduced waiting times"). Premium/paid users get priority in the queue. Filters (gender, country) are sent to the server via a FILTER_UPDATE message. The server then pushes a CALL_REQUEST message to both matched clients with each other's clientId and countryCode. One client will receive an INIT message instructing it to begin the WebRTC handshake as the offerer.

6. WebRTC Call Setup (Peer-to-Peer Audio)
Once matched, the signaling server acts as a relay to set up the direct WebRTC peer connection between the two clients. The sequence is:
Client A (Offerer)                  Signaling Server              Client B (Answerer)
     |                                     |                              |
     |------ CALL_REQUEST ---------------->|                              |
     |                                     |------- CALL_REQUEST -------->|
     |<------ INIT (you are offerer) ------|                              |
     |                                     |<------ CALL_RESPONSE --------|
     | createOffer()                       |                              |
     | setLocalDescription(offer)          |                              |
     |------ SDP {sdpType:"OFFER"} ------->|                              |
     |                                     |------- SDP (OFFER) --------->|
     |                                     |                 setRemoteDescription(offer)
     |                                     |                 createAnswer()
     |                                     |                 setLocalDescription(answer)
     |                                     |<------ SDP {sdpType:"ANSWER"}|
     |<------ SDP (ANSWER) ----------------|                              |
     | setRemoteDescription(answer)        |                              |
     |                                     |                              |
     |------ CANDIDATE (ICE) ------------>|------- CANDIDATE ----------->|
     |<------ CANDIDATE (ICE) ------------|<------ CANDIDATE ------------|
     |                                     |                              |
     |============== Direct P2P Audio Stream (WebRTC) ==================>|

