## 8. Audio Moderation Pipeline

Running **in parallel** with every active call:
```
Microphone (getUserMedia)
    ↓
AudioContext (samples audio stream in chunks)
    ↓
Buffer: collectedAudioData[] / collectedSamples counter
    ↓ (when buffer ready, beingSent flag = true)
POST https://voice-mod.airtalk.live/moderation
    → Server-side moderation for policy violations

Simultaneously:
POST https://ai.airtalk.live/analyze
    → AI model content analysis
```

- Designed to detect explicit/harmful audio in real time
- Audio is **not stored** for calls — only sampled for moderation
- `VOICE_MOD_URL` constant is hardcoded in the Angular service

---

## 9. Call Termination
```
Either party clicks "Hang Up"
    → Client sends: { messageType: "HANG_UP" }
    → Remote client receives HANG_UP via WebSocket
    → Both: CallStatusService.emitDisconnected()
    → Both: RTCPeerConnection torn down
    → Both: _isInCall = false
    → UI returns to idle state ("Tap the Call button...")
    → Server clears the active call session
```

- Server can also force a disconnect via `HANG_UP` from its side
- Reconnection logic triggered via `RECONNECT` message
- Connection health monitored via `setupConnectionChecker()`

