## 11. Key Design Decisions

| Decision | Rationale |
|---|---|
| **No third-party SDK** | Raw WebRTC APIs give full control; avoids per-minute Agora/Twilio costs |
| **Single WebSocket for everything** | Auth, matchmaking, signaling, presence, system msgs — no REST polling needed |
| **P2P media flow** | Voice goes browser-to-browser after handshake; dramatically reduces server bandwidth and latency |
| **Self-hosted TURN** | coturn on Hetzner — cost-effective; time-limited HMAC prevents credential abuse |
| **Server-side audio moderation** | Safety/compliance for a stranger-calling platform without storing full recordings |
| **Premium queue priority** | Monetization lever; faster matches for paying users incentivizes upgrades |
| **Angular 14 + RxJS** | Observable streams cleanly model the async, event-driven nature of WebRTC calls |

